This is a basic 3D printed case of the Estardyn DIY FM Radio Receiver Kit Wireless Stereo PCB Module 76-108MHz DC 1.8-3.6V found on online shopping stores like AliExpress. 
https://www.aliexpress.us/item/3256812394028403.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com

- All info resources necessary to print this case are available in this repository (message if not and I will add them).
- There exists no commit history here because I manually version controlled without Git (should have just used Git). 
- The top clip FreeCAD file got messed up somehow and it's just solid without editable subpieces. This would have been prevented had I used Git during the length of the project. 

Printing Recommendations: 
- After printing, it's going to be pretty hard to get the supports off. I recommend using some flush clippers and goggles to cut and peel off the supports. The models are all in positions that use the least amount of supports already. 
- Make sure that near the headphone hole, the one that goes through one of the top clips, that you don't pull it off when pulling off the supports. It's a lot stronger than the supports but one might pull it off without thinking about it. 

Materials:
- Used PLA 2.0+ 1.75mm (some others may not be strong enough - use at discretion). 
- Used Flashforge AD5X 3D printer

Slicer Settings:
The settings are a part of the sliced file. Here's a summary below:
- UltiMaker Cura
    - 60mm/sec base extruder movement speed (qualitative - go faster if you like, I just did this to avoid errors from going too fast)
    - 220C Extruder temperature
    - 60C Base pad temperature
